rs tightly around 28–31°C because short-range forecast models show Beijing under a weakening subtropical high with variable moisture influx from the East Asian monsoon.** Ensemble guidance from global and regional models indicates daytime maxima near 29°C on July 24, tempered by expected cloud cover and scattered showers typical of the late-July rainy period. Small differences in simulated timing and intensity of precipitation or boundary-layer mixing produce the 1–2 °C spread across leading outcomes; drier, sunnier solutions push probabilities toward 30–31 °C while stronger afternoon convection favors the lower side. Historical climatology places late-July Beijing highs near 31 °C, but current moisture anomalies and urban heat-island modulation introduce measurable uncertainty that traders price as near-even odds among the top four bins. Updated model runs and official China Meteorological Administration guidance over the next 48 hours will be the key near-term drivers of any further shifts.","context_requires_regen":true,"context_updated_at":"2026-07-22T05:00:13.228Z"}}],"ready":false,"funded":false,"acceptingOrdersTimestamp":"2026-07-22T04:03:30Z","cyom":false,"competitive":0.8003199679231757,"pagerDutyNotificationEnabled":false,"approved":true,"rewardsMinSize":20,"rewardsMaxSpread":4.5,"spread":0.001,"lastTradePrice":0.001,"bestAsk":0.001,"automaticallyActive":true,"clearBookOnStart":false,"manualActivation":false,"negRiskOther":false,"umaResolutionStatuses":"[]","pendingDeployment":false,"deploying":false,"deployingTimestamp":"2026-07-22T04:03:15.342145Z","rfqEnabled":false,"holdingRewardsEnabled":false,"feesEnabled":true,"requiresTranslation":false,"feeType":"weather_fees","feeSchedule":{"exponent":1,"rate":0.05,"takerOnly":true,"rebateRate":0.25}}
